    <briefdescription>
<para><ref refid="structllvm_1_1object_1_1_chained_fixup_target" kindref="compound">ChainedFixupTarget</ref> holds all the information about an external symbol necessary to bind this binary to that symbol. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>These values are referenced indirectly by chained fixup binds. This structure captures values from all import and symbol formats.</para>
<para>Be aware there are two notions of weak here: WeakImport == true The associated bind may be set to 0 if this symbol is missing from its parent library. This is called a &quot;weak import.&quot; LibOrdinal == BIND_SPECIAL_DYLIB_WEAK_LOOKUP This symbol may be coalesced with other libraries vending the same symbol. E.g., C++&apos;s &quot;operator new&quot;. This is called a &quot;weak bind.&quot; </para>
    </detaileddescription>
